WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.967
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:15.031
Unit four: Nature & Environment. In this unit, you will talk about how to protect nature.

4
00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:16.809
Forest.

5
00:00:17.509 --> 00:00:20.112
Forest means a large area full of trees.

6
00:00:20.412 --> 00:00:22.214
Elephants live in the forest.

7
00:00:22.914 --> 00:00:25.613
Your turn. Say: Forest.

8
00:00:28.313 --> 00:00:29.210
Forest.

9
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:30.951
River.

10
00:00:31.651 --> 00:00:34.823
River means a long line of water that flows to the sea.

11
00:00:35.123 --> 00:00:36.890
Don't throw rubbish in the river.

12
00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.289
Your turn. Say: River.

13
00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:43.781
River.

14
00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:45.703
Pollution.

15
00:00:46.403 --> 00:00:50.272
Pollution means dirty air, water or land that harms living things.

16
00:00:50.572 --> 00:00:52.235
Pollution makes the river dirty.

17
00:00:52.935 --> 00:00:56.284
Your turn. Say: Pollution.

18
00:00:58.984 --> 00:00:59.880
Pollution.

19
00:01:00.883 --> 00:01:01.896
Recycle.

20
00:01:02.596 --> 00:01:05.687
Recycle means to use old things to make new things.

21
00:01:05.987 --> 00:01:07.894
We recycle plastic bottles.

22
00:01:08.594 --> 00:01:12.105
Your turn. Say: Recycle.

23
00:01:14.805 --> 00:01:15.783
Recycle.

24
00:01:16.783 --> 00:01:17.703
Protect.

25
00:01:18.403 --> 00:01:20.600
Protect means to keep something safe.

26
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.923
We must protect wild animals.

27
00:01:23.623 --> 00:01:26.078
Your turn. Say: Protect.

28
00:01:28.778 --> 00:01:29.709
Protect.

29
00:01:30.717 --> 00:01:31.718
Wildlife.

30
00:01:32.418 --> 00:01:35.334
Wildlife means animals and plants that live in nature.

31
00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.669
Cambodia has amazing wildlife.

32
00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:41.578
Your turn. Say: Wildlife.

33
00:01:44.278 --> 00:01:45.280
Wildlife.

34
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:47.575
Species.

35
00:01:48.275 --> 00:01:51.528
Species means a group of animals or plants of the same type.

36
00:01:51.828 --> 00:01:53.677
There are many bird species here.

37
00:01:54.377 --> 00:01:56.785
Your turn. Say: Species.

38
00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:00.556
Species.

39
00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:02.458
Endangered.

40
00:02:03.158 --> 00:02:05.460
Endangered means almost gone from the world.

41
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.388
The tiger is endangered.

42
00:02:08.088 --> 00:02:10.833
Your turn. Say: Endangered.

43
00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.499
Endangered.

44
00:02:15.483 --> 00:02:16.728
Habitat loss.

45
00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:20.925
Habitat loss means when animals lose the places where they live.

46
00:02:21.225 --> 00:02:23.306
Cutting trees causes habitat loss.

47
00:02:24.006 --> 00:02:26.972
Your turn. Say: Habitat loss.

48
00:02:29.672 --> 00:02:30.952
Habitat loss.

49
00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.090
Plant a tree.

50
00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.347
Plant a tree means to put a young tree in the ground.

51
00:02:36.647 --> 00:02:38.298
Let's plant a tree at school.

52
00:02:38.998 --> 00:02:42.336
Your turn. Say: Plant a tree.

53
00:02:45.036 --> 00:02:46.141
Plant a tree.

54
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.337
Clean energy.

55
00:02:49.037 --> 00:02:53.335
Clean energy means power from the sun, wind or water that doesn't pollute.

56
00:02:53.635 --> 00:02:55.913
Solar panels make clean energy.

57
00:02:56.613 --> 00:02:59.324
Your turn. Say: Clean energy.

58
00:03:02.024 --> 00:03:03.153
Clean energy.

59
00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:04.861
Litter.

60
00:03:05.561 --> 00:03:08.002
Litter means rubbish left on the ground.

61
00:03:08.302 --> 00:03:09.744
Pick up the litter, please.

62
00:03:10.444 --> 00:03:12.922
Your turn. Say: Litter.

63
00:03:15.622 --> 00:03:16.426
Litter.

64
00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:19.393
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:19.693 --> 00:03:22.134
Sreypich, why are some animals endangered?

66
00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.647
Because of habitat loss and pollution.

67
00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.172
What should we do?

68
00:03:29.483 --> 00:03:31.529
We should recycle and plant trees.

69
00:03:32.817 --> 00:03:34.468
And what must we never do?

70
00:03:35.783 --> 00:03:37.841
We must never drop litter in the river!

71
00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.649
Grammar focus: should and must.

72
00:03:41.949 --> 00:03:44.764
We should recycle. We must protect wildlife.

73
00:03:45.064 --> 00:03:48.865
'Must' is stronger than 'should'. 'Mustn't' means it is not allowed.

74
00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.642
Now read and listen. Saving Our Forests.

75
00:03:52.942 --> 00:03:56.044
Cambodia has beautiful forests, rivers and wildlife.

76
00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:00.778
But pollution and habitat loss put many species in danger.

77
00:04:02.083 --> 00:04:05.662
Some animals, like the tiger and the elephant, are endangered.

78
00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.878
We should recycle, use clean energy and plant trees.

79
00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:13.345
We must protect nature for the future.

80
00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.384
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:17.684 --> 00:04:19.857
We blank protect endangered animals.

82
00:04:20.157 --> 00:04:23.428
A, must. B, musts. C, to must.

83
00:04:27.417 --> 00:04:28.998
The answer is A: must.

84
00:04:30.483 --> 00:04:32.460
Rubbish left on the ground is blank.

85
00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.775
A, litter. B, wildlife. C, energy.

86
00:04:39.783 --> 00:04:41.411
The answer is A: litter.

87
00:04:42.917 --> 00:04:45.172
Almost gone from the world means blank.

88
00:04:45.472 --> 00:04:50.356
A, endangered. B, protected. C, recycled.

89
00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.698
The answer is A: endangered.

90
00:04:58.183 --> 00:05:01.799
Now it's your turn to speak. How can we protect the environment?

91
00:05:07.099 --> 00:05:11.749
We should recycle plastic and plant trees. We must not throw rubbish in rivers.

92
00:05:12.049 --> 00:05:13.677
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:14.683 --> 00:05:18.903
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and should and must.

94
00:05:19.203 --> 00:05:23.736
Today's value is caring for nature. Care for plants, birds and our planet.

95
00:05:24.036 --> 00:05:26.630
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

96
00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.548
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

